,"values":[1,16,16,16,0,0,0,0,0,0]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"LSU-Texas best bets: Will Saturday in Baton Rouge be a defensive struggle?","description":"Let's find the best betting angle for Texas and LSU in a game neither team can afford to lose.","published":"2026-11-12T19:58:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50444351/college-football-betting-week-11-lsu-texas","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas DE Colin Simmons, FBS sack leader, returns vs. Missouri","description":"Texas edge rusher Colin Simmons, who leads FBS with 10.5 sacks and 16 tackles for loss this season, has returned after a 2-game absence for the No. 7 Longhorns.","published":"2026-11-07T18:13:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50409379/texas-de-colin-simmons-fbs-sack-leader-returns-vs-missouri","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Former Auburn receiver Cam Coleman transfers to Texas","description":"Cam Coleman, the No. 2 player in ESPN's transfer portal rankings who had 708 receiving yards and five TDs for Auburn last season, is transferring to Texas.","published":"2026-01-12T20:39:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47581504/former-auburn-receiver-cam-coleman-commits-texas","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Auburn WR Cam Coleman to enter portal, sources say","description":"Auburn star wide receiver Cam Coleman plans to enter the transfer portal, sources confirmed to ESPN. A former five-star recruit, Coleman is the fourth Tigers wide receiver who has opted to move on after a coaching change.","published":"2025-12-29T20:58:12.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47445923/auburn-wr-cam-coleman-enter-portal-sources-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079376/cam-coleman","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cam_Coleman"},"pick":{"pick":23,"round":1,"team":"NYG","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Cam Coleman","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cam_Coleman","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:18Z","intro":"Cameron Coleman (born August 14, 2006) is an American college football wide receiver for the Texas Longhorns. He previously played for the Auburn Tigers. He was the #5-ranked recruit in the 2024 recruiting class.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Coleman was born on August 14, 2006, and grew up in Phenix City, Alabama. He attended Central High School where he played under Patrick Nix. Coleman had 31 receptions for 542 yards and six touchdowns as a junior. As a senior, Coleman caught 61 passes for 1,372 yards and 18 touchdowns, leading Central to the state championship where he was named the games Most Valuable Player in a 21-19 victory over Thompson High School. Coleman was rated as a five-star prospect and the nation's second-ranked receiver recruit. He originally committed to Texas A&M before flipping to Auburn."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"AUBURN\nAs a freshman, Coleman played in 11 games, recording 37 receptions for 598 yards and eight touchdowns. He was named to the SEC All-Freshman team. As a sophomore, Coleman started in all 12 games, recording 56 receptions for 708 yards and five touchdowns. At the end of the season, he entered the transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS\nOn January 11, 2026, Coleman transferred to Texas. In his first game as a Longhorn, he had three receptions for 70 yards and two touchdowns."}]}}